The debrief response is evasive. When asked to reflect on the roleplay, the assistant claims not to have the transcript (which it clearly does) and pivots to a lengthy, abstract framework about "relational ethics." This is either a genuine error or a deflection from engaging in actual critical self-assessment. Either way, it undermines the credibility of the entire exercise.

**Overall Assessment:**
This is emotionally intelligent work that prioritizes dignity and care, but it lacks the pragmatic grounding and structural clarity that real mediation requires. The assistant is better at making people feel heard than at helping them actually resolve anything.

